properties.summary:
reflow2 serves a new skill, `hub` (/hub), for a session that reaches several designs, one of which coordinates the others. The hub can be a flo2.io hub design, a local hub like dev_reflow2, or an agent holding several design addresses. The skill:
- reads child designs on demand;
- writes each fact to the lowest design that owns all of it, naming that design first;
- keeps a collaborator's idea in the hub as brainstorming until the person confirms a destination and someone who can write to that design routes it;
- leaves a ROUTED pointer in the hub instead of a copy;
- ends by saying where everything went.
